            <history xml:id="history_176N200D1">
               <p xml:id="idm69">Johannes Frederik Frøhlich (1806-1860), for whose album this canon was written, was a Danish composer, violinist and conductor. From 1827 he was permanently appointed at The Royal Theatre where he became chief conductor in 1836. The same year he was co-founder of Musikforeningen. His brother Franz had been Hartmann's violin teacher.</p>
